# Database migrations

Schema changes are managed with [Alembic](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/).

## Commands

Run from `backend/`:

```bash
# Apply all pending migrations
uv run alembic upgrade head

# Show current revision
uv run alembic current

# Autogenerate after model changes (review output before committing)
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

# Roll back one revision (staging only — test before prod)
uv run alembic downgrade -1
```

## Environment

- Uses `DATABASE_URL` from `.env` / environment (same as the app).
- Override for CI or one-off runs: `ALEMBIC_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://…`
- Migration commands use sync `psycopg`; the app runtime stays on `asyncpg`.

## Bootstrap existing dev databases

If tables were created with `create_all` and already match the initial migration:

```bash
uv run alembic stamp head
```

Fresh databases should use `upgrade head` instead.

Tests and local bootstrap use `ensure_migrated()` in application code, which stamps legacy
schemas automatically when app tables exist but `alembic_version` is missing.

## Production rules

See **Production migration rules** in `backend/backend.md`. Summary: never rewrite applied migrations,
one change per revision, migrate before restart, backup before prod upgrade, review all autogen output.
